# Locally: copy this file to .env and edit the values, then rebuild.
# On Vercel: add the same names under Settings -> Environment Variables, then
# REDEPLOY — these values are baked in at build time, so an existing
# deployment keeps the old ones until it is rebuilt.
#
# Each name below also works with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix (e.g.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VISION_PDF_URL), whichever your host lets you type.
#
# Everything here ends up visible to visitors in the page — never put a
# password or a secret key in these.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "اكتشف رؤيتنا" button
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Link opened by the vision button on the home page. Change it whenever the
# PDF is replaced. If left empty the button falls back to the current file.
VISION_PDF_URL=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "انضم إلينا" register button
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "true" shows the register button on the home page. Anything else (or leaving
# it out) hides the button and makes /join unreachable.
REGISTRATION_ENABLED="false"

# Where the register button sends people. Put your Google Form link here and
# it opens in a new tab. Leave it empty to use the site's own /join form
# instead — that one stores applications in MongoDB and needs MONGODB_URI.
REGISTER_URL=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database (only needed for the built-in /join form and partner enquiries)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave MONGODB_URI empty while no database is attached: the site builds and
# runs fine without it, and the forms answer "unavailable" instead of failing.
MONGODB_URI=""
